    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_85a66dcb",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: that's right white crackers; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image shows a simple white plate with white crackers, overlaid with the text 'that's right white crackers.' The overall intent is to use the visual of plain white crackers to make a pun or joke about 'white' being associated with something bland, generic, or unremarkable. The meme is not inherently toxic or harmful; it relies on a play on words rather than targeting any specific group. The term 'white crackers' is not a racial slur or stereotype in this context, but rather a literal description of the food item. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of the mundane food item with the phrase 'that's right,' which implies a sarcastic or self-aware acknowledgment of the obviousness or banality of the subject. There is no evidence of abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda intent. The meme is a light-hearted, wordplay-based joke without any toxic or harmful content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a1848535"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
