      "instance_name": "sarcastic_irony",
      "label": "sarcastic acknowledgment of banality",
      "description": "The phrase 'that's right white crackers' expresses a sarcastic or self-aware acknowledgment that the crackers are so plain and unremarkable that it's obvious or even boring — a humorous exaggeration of the mundane. This emotion is conveyed through the juxtaposition of the literal food item with the rhetorical phrase, implying a mocking or ironic tone.",
